<article class="env-lemma" id="09VB">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09VB">Lemma <span data-tag="09VB">36.12.6</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a finite morphism of schemes such that $f_*\mathcal{O}_ X$ is pseudo-coherent as an $\mathcal{O}_ Y$-module<a class="footnotemark" href="#a0000790956" id="a0000790956-mark"><sup>1</sup></a>. Let $E \in D_\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$. Then $E$ is $m$-pseudo-coherent if and only if $Rf_*E$ is $m$-pseudo-coherent. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a translation of More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/064Z" data-tag="064Z">15.66.11</a> into the language of schemes. To do the translation, use Lemmas <a href="/tag/06Z0" data-tag="06Z0">36.3.5</a> and <a href="/tag/08E7" data-tag="08E7">36.10.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>